WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.050
Which cloud you're in changes the answer.

2
00:00:02.050 --> 00:00:08.056
For interactive sign-in, a CRL must stay
under twenty megabytes in public Entra ID,

3
00:00:08.056 --> 00:00:14.062
which includes GCC, and forty-five in Azure
US Government, which includes GCC High.

4
00:00:14.062 --> 00:00:16.912
Either way it must download
within ten seconds.

5
00:00:16.912 --> 00:00:20.112
So the expected-configuration
file holds both sets,

6
00:00:20.112 --> 00:00:23.013
and the check takes a
cloud name with no default.

7
00:00:23.013 --> 00:00:25.451
Learn doesn't say which megabyte it means,

8
00:00:25.451 --> 00:00:29.380
so the configuration reads the
decimal one, the stricter reading.
